  pages     = "2847--2861",
  abstract  = "Predicting bacteriophage infection of specific bacterial strains
               promises advancements in phage therapy and microbial ecology.
               Whether the dynamics of well-established phage-host model systems
               generalize to the wide diversity of microbes is currently
               unknown. Here we show that we could accurately predict the
               outcomes of phage-bacteria interactions at the strain level in
               natural isolates from the genus Escherichia using only genomic
               data (area under the receiver operating characteristic curve
