  number    =  7,
  pages     = "btad409",
  abstract  = "Abstract Summary With recent advances in sequencing technologies,
               it is now possible to obtain near-perfect complete bacterial
               chromosome assemblies cheaply and efficiently by combining a
               long-read-first assembly approach with short-read polishing.
               However, existing methods for assembling bacterial plasmids from
               long-read-first assemblies often misassemble or even miss
               bacterial plasmids entirely and accordingly require manual
               curation. Plassembler was developed to provide a tool that
               automatically assembles and outputs bacterial plasmids using a
               hybrid assembly approach. It achieves increased accuracy and
               computational efficiency compared to the existing gold standard
               tool Unicycler by removing chromosomal reads from the input read
               sets using a mapping approach. Availability and implementation
               Plassembler is implemented in Python and is installable as a
               bioconda package using ‘conda install -c bioconda plassembler’.
               The source code is available on GitHub at
