               and tissue biopsy samples show that hydrogenase-encoding genes
               are widely present and transcribed in gut bacteria. Assessment of
               19 taxonomically diverse gut isolates revealed that the group B
               [FeFe]-hydrogenases produce large amounts of H 2 gas and support
