  volume      =  8,
  number      =  11,
  pages       = "2170--2182",
  abstract    = "Methanogenic archaea are major producers of methane, a potent
                 greenhouse gas and biofuel, and are widespread in diverse
                 environments, including the animal gut. The ecophysiology of
                 methanogens is likely impacted by viruses, which remain,
                 however, largely uncharacterized. Here we carried out a global
